# SHA-256 of every file of the Ubuntu Touch build an image is made from, as tools/ut-fetch.sh lays
# them out (build/ut/<build>/, the Android images in android/). tools/ut-fetch.sh checks each file
# before it uses it (also one that is already there), tools/boot-files.sh the three boot images
# and image/mkimage.sh the images it is given; a file that differs stops the run. The boot images
# whole, not only the kernel and ramdisks tools/boot-files.sha256 compares: their headers carry
# the kernel command line, the DTB and the bootconfig.
# A new UT build needs a new plinius-kmod and new lines in tools/boot-files.sha256 first, then the
# build id and the lines here.
# build 04112026
